---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import Photo from '@/components/Photo.astro';
import Arrow from '@/components/Arrow.astro';
import { kwacha, percent, pricing } from '@/data/site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="The Dottra credit facility"
  heading="One credit limit you can use more than once."
  description="Dottra is a reusable credit facility for eligible salaried workers and sponsored students in Zambia. Draw to mobile money, pay back any time, and receive one statement a month."
  eyebrow="Product"
  summary="Dottra gives you a credit limit after we check who you are and what you can afford. You draw from it when you need to, pay it back when you can, and draw again."
  ogImage="/og/product.png"
>
  <div class="content-stack">
    <Section title="What you get">
      <p>
        A credit facility with one limit. Inside the app you can always see your <strong>credit limit</strong>, your
        <strong>available credit</strong> (the part you can still draw), and your <strong>outstanding balance</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        You don't apply each time you need money. Once your limit is set, a draw takes a few seconds and goes to the mobile
        money number registered in your name.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Draw the amount you need">
      <p>
        You choose the amount: anything from {kwacha(pricing.minimumDraw)} up to your available credit, to the ngwee.
        There are no fixed packages to pick from.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before you confirm, the app shows how much will be added to your balance, the processing fee, and exactly how much
        will arrive on mobile money. You confirm with your PIN or fingerprint.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Pay back on your schedule">
      <p>
        You can pay any amount from {kwacha(pricing.minimumPayment)} (or the full balance, if it's less), on any day, from
        mobile money. As you pay back what you drew, your available credit goes back up.
      </p>
      <p>
        The monthly charge is worked out on your average daily balance, so paying back earlier costs less. There's no
        charge for paying early.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="One statement a month">
      <p>
        If you owe anything at the end of a calendar month, the app produces a statement. It lists your draws, payments
        and the monthly charge, and gives a payment due date {pricing.gracePeriodDays} days after the statement date.
      </p>
      <p>If you owe nothing, there's no statement and no charge.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="What it costs">
      <ul>
        <li>A processing fee of {percent(pricing.processingFeeRate)} of each draw, minimum {kwacha(pricing.processingFeeMinimum)}, taken from the amount you receive.</li>
        <li>A monthly charge of {percent(pricing.monthlyChargeRate)} of your average daily balance for the month.</li>
        <li>No sign-up, membership or late fees.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a class="text-link text-link-with-icon" href="/pricing/"><span>See pricing with worked examples</span><Arrow /></a></p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="If a statement goes overdue">
      <p>
        If a statement isn't paid by the end of its due date, the facility is temporarily frozen. You can't draw while it's
        frozen, but you can still pay. Once the overdue amount is paid, it unfreezes automatically.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="What Dottra is not">
      <p>
        It's not a savings account, and it's not meant for borrowing over many months. It works best for short gaps: a cost
        that arrives before your salary or allowance does, which you can pay back within a few weeks.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you find yourself drawing every month to cover the same shortfall, that's a budget problem that credit will make
        worse. Our guide to <a href="/blog/use-a-credit-line-with-a-plan/">using a credit facility without falling behind</a> covers this.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Security">
      <p>
        Every draw needs your PIN or fingerprint. Money is only ever sent to the mobile money number registered in your
        name. The app doesn't ask for access to your contacts, photos or messages.
      </p>
      <p>
        Dottra staff will never ask for your PIN, password or a one-time code, by phone, SMS, WhatsApp or email.
      </p>
    </Section>
  </div>

  <div class="page-photo">
    <Photo name="cairo-road-mobile-money" sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 560px" />
  </div>

  <div class="action-row">
    <a class="button" href="/how-it-works/"><span>How it works, step by step</span><Arrow /></a>
    <a class="button button-secondary" href="/eligibility/"><span>Who can apply</span><Arrow /></a>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
